Then Jesus left the people and went to Bethany, and he spent the night there. The fig tree that was cursed
Early in the morning, Jesus was returning to Jerusalem. He was hungry.
A man saw a pistachio tree by the road. He approached the tree, but found only leaves on it. Then he said to it: "Never produce fruit again!" Suddenly the tree dried up.
When the Muslims saw this, they were shaken and said, "How has the fruit tree dried up so quickly?"
Jesus answered, "What I tell you is true. You must believe and not doubt. Then you can do what he did to the fig tree. And you can say to this mountain, 'Be gone and cast yourself into the sea,' and it will be done."
If you believe, you will receive what you ask for in your prayers." "It questions the authority of Christ"
Jesus entered the passageway of his mosque. While he was teaching there, the leaders and elders of the people came to him. "By what authority are you doing these things?" they asked. "Who gave you this authority?"
Jesus answered: "I will ask you one question. If you answer me, then I will tell you the context of the authority under which I do these things."
From where did the gospel of John come? Did it come from heaven? Or did it come from men?" They discussed this among themselves. And they said, "If we say, 'From heaven,' he will say, 'Why then did you not believe him?'"
But what if we say: "Who of the men?" We fear the people. Everyone believes that John was a prophet.
They answered Jesus, "We do not know." And Jesus said, "Neither will I tell you by what authority I do these things. The Parable of the Two Sons"
What do you think about this? There was a man who had two sons. He went to the first one and said, "Son, go today and start working in the farm."
"I will do that," the son replied. But later he changed his mind and went.
Then the father went to the other son, and said the same thing to him. The son replied, "I will, sir." But he did not go.
Which of the two sons did the will of his father?" They said, "The first son." Jesus said to them, "The very truth I tell you is this. Tax collectors and prostitutes will enter the Kingdom of God before you do."
John came to show you the correct way to live. And you did not believe in him. But the Muslims and the Bokkats believed. You saw that. But even that did not empty your sins and wish for him. The story of the Muslims.
Listen to another story. A man owned a plot of land, and he set up a vidya farm. He put a wall around it. He created a pit to make wine in. He also built a watchtower. Then he rented out his farm to some farmers. Then he left on a trip.
When the time for storage approached, a man sent his workers to the lessors. He instructed the workers to gather his share of the fruits.
But the renters took his servants, beat one of them, killed another, and threw stones at a third to kill him.
Then the man sent other servants for rent. He sent more than he sent the first time. And they treated them the same way.
In the end, he sent his son to him. He said, "They will respect my son."
But the tenants saw the Son coming. And they said to one another, "This is the Heir! Come, let's kill him and take possession of his property!"
So they took him and left with him from noon. Then they killed him.
When the owner of the field returns, what will he do to those who are operating it?
"The bad people will be destroyed," they replied. "Then the farm will be rented to other tenants, and they will give him their share of the crop at harvest time."
Jesus said to them, "Have you never read in the scriptures: 'The stone which the builders rejected has become the chief cornerstone. This was done by the Lord, and it is amazing in our eyes'? (Psalm 118:22, 23)"
So, here is what I tell you: the kingdom of God will be taken away from you, and it will be given to people who produce its results.
Everyone who falls on that stone will be broken into pieces. But the stone will break anyone who falls on it.
The chiefs and Pharisees listened to Jesus' stories. They knew he was talking about them.
Therefore, they looked for a way to arrest him, but they were afraid of the crowds. And the people believed that Jesus was a prophet.
The Wedding Dinner Story
Tell them other stories. And he said:
Here is like the Kingdom of Heaven. A king prepared a dinner for his son.
He sent a man of his servants to one who was invited to dinner. He told them to come, but they refused.
Then he sent two other messengers. He said, "Inform those who have been invited that I have prepared my meal. My oxen have been killed and their largest loads have been carried. Everything is ready. Go to the wedding feast."
But people did not pay attention. One went to his field. Another went to his work.
The rest preyed upon his worshippers, treated them badly, and then killed them.
The king became very angry, and sent his army to destroy them. They killed those criminals and burned their city.
The king said to his servants, "The dinner is ready. But those I invited were not worthy to attend."
I am going to the main corners, and let everyone you find bring the dinner.
Therefore, the slaves went out into the streets, and gathered together all the people that they found, whether they were good or bad. And very quickly the place that had been prepared for the feast became full of guests.
The king came to see the guests, and he noticed a man there who was not dressed in wedding clothes.
"My friend," he asked, "how did you get here without wedding clothes?" The man had not thought of anything he could say.
And the king told his servants: "Tie his hands and feet, and forget him outside in the dark, for the people will weep and gnash their teeth there."
Many are called, but few are chosen." Is it impossible to pay taxes to Caesar?
The Pharisees went out and planned to entangle Him in His own words.
They sent their followers to him, and they sent along those who continued in the Herodian covenant. And they said, "Our teacher, we know that you are a man of honor. You teach the way of God in truth. You do not allow others to tell you what you should do or say. And you do not care how important the one is who speaks to you."
And they said, "What then is your opinion? Is it lawful to give tribute to Caesar, or not?"
But Jesus knew their wicked plans. And he said, "You are the deniers! Why do you seek to entrap me?"
Show me the machine that people use to pay taxes. And they showed him a machine made of silver.
He asked them, "Whose image is this? And whose words?"
"Caesar's property," they replied. Then he said to them, "Give to Caesar what belongs to Caesar, and give to God what belongs to God."
When they heard that, they were shaken, so they departed from it and went away. The wedding, when the dead rise.
On the same day, Sadducees came to Jesus with a question. They do not believe that people rise from the dead.
"Doctor," they said, "This is what we told Moses. If a man dies without having children, his wife must be taken from his sister. And he must have children so that the name of his brother may be completed."
There were seven brothers among us. The first one got married, then he died, and he left no children behind him, so he left his wife for his brother.
The same thing happened with the second and third brothers. And it happened until it reached the seventh brother.
In the end, the lady died.
Now, when the dead rise, to whom will his wife belong? All seven were married to her.
Jesus answered, "You are wrong, because you do not know the Scriptures, nor the power of God."
When the dead rise, they will not be given in marriage, nor will the parents of the dead be given in marriage. They will be like the angels in heaven.
What about resurrection from the dead? Have you not read what God has said to you?
He said, "I am God, whom God had made servants; I am God, whom Isaac was; and I am God, whom Jacob was." (Doctrine and Covenants 3:6) He is not the God in whom the dead believe, but is the God in whom the living believe."
When the people heard this, they were astonished at what he had learned. The most important commands
Alvares listened until the two Sadducees did not have an answer for Jesus. So Alvares came to coordinate.
One of them, a legal expert, tested Jesus with a question.
"Doctor," he asked, "what is the most important thing about law?"
Jesus answered, "You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul and with all your mind." (Dori 6:5)
This is the first and primary command.
And the second is like it: 'Love your neighbor as yourself.' (Luke 18:19)
All that is stated in the law and the apostles is built upon these two commandments. Who is the Christ?
The Pharisees were gathered together. And Jesus asked them:
What do you think about the Messiah? Who is his son? "The son of David," they answered.
He said to them, "Then, why does David call him 'Lord'? The Holy Spirit spoke through David himself. David said:"
The Lord said to my Lord, "Sit at my right hand until I make your enemies your footstool." (Psalm 110:1)
So, if David called him "Lord," how can he be David's son?
No one could answer him with a single word. And from that day on, no one dared to ask him any questions.
Jesus is tried by the Pharisees and experts in the law.
Did Jesus not say to the multitude and to whom does Jesus belong?
"The law teachers and the Pharisees sit in the seat of Moses," he said.
So, you must obey them and do everything they tell you. But don't do what they do. They don't practice what they preach.
They are tied to heavy weights and carried on people's shoulders, but they do not wish to raise a single hand to carry them.
Everything they do is done so that others may see them. They place on their father and on themselves small boxes containing verses from the suras. They make these boxes very wide, and they make the twigs attached to their garments very long.
They like to sit in the place of honor at meals. They also like to get the most important places in the synagogues.
They like to be summoned to shopping malls. They like to be called "Lord" by people.
But do not call yourselves "Lord." You have one continuing Lord, and you are all brothers.
Do not call anyone on earth "father". You have one Father, and He is in heaven.
You should not be called "master". You have only one master, that is, the Christ.
The most important person among you will be your worship.
He who exalts himself shall be abased; and he who humbles himself shall be exalted.
How close will it be to you, you teachers of the law and you, prey! You are the deceived ones! You have shut the kingdom of heaven in the faces of people. You neither enter yourselves, nor do you allow anyone else to enter.
