How much of a tragedy it was for you, people of the Sharia and Persianism! Your lies! You wander everywhere to attract someone to your faith. Then you make him a father for a more intense sanctity than you are.
How bitter it is for you, you who continue to see! You say: 'If someone takes the promise in the name of the mosque, he means nothing, but whoever takes the promise in the name of silver in his mosque, the promise is due.'" Here is the translation without any additional text: How bitter it is for you, you who continue to see! You say: 'If someone takes the promise in the name of the mosque, he means nothing, but whoever takes the promise in the name of silver in his mosque, the promise is due.'"
You are neglectful and despairing! What is more important? Is it gold? Or is it the mosque that makes gold forbidden?
You also say, "If one of them takes a vow in the name of the altar, it is nothing, but if one takes a vow in the name of the gift offered over him, the vow shall be binding."
O blind one! Which is more important? Is it the gift or the altar that sanctifies the gift?
So, whoever is promised in the name of the worshipper, is promised in their name and everything on that worshipper.
And whoever takes a covenant in the name of the mosque, takes a covenant in His name and in the name of what exists within it.
And everyone who takes the covenant in the name of the heavens has taken the covenant in the name of God's grace, which extends to everyone.
How it has been an eye-opener for you, O teachers of the law and you, the prey! You are the ones who have been deceived! You give God ten from your finds, like a miner, a delver, and a prospector. But you have not beenware of the weighty matters which are clearly stated in the law of God, like justice, mercy, and truth. You should beware of the last weighty matters without presuming upon the first weighty matters."
You blind guides! You filter out a gnat from your drink, but you swallow a camel whole!
How much of a tragedy it was for you, you people of the laws and the knightly code! Your lies! You clean the outside of the cup and the dish, but on the inside you are filled with jealousy. You desire only to satisfy your cravings.
My translation is swallowed! Wash first the place of the ball and the belly, then the place will be washed flat.
How much of a tragedy it was for you, people of the Sharia and Persianate! Your lies! Like the towers called the White. They look beautiful on the outside, but on the inside they are full of the bones of the dead. They are also full of other things that are not clean and pure.
This is how it is with you. From the outside, it looks like you are doing what is right, but on the inside, you are filled with things that are wrong. You show what you do not possess.
How bitter it is for you, oh law teachers and prey! You are the abandoners! You are building the tombs of the apostles. You are calling the mysteries of the believers.
And you say, "Indeed, we did not act as they acted during the days of those who preceded us. We did not do what they did. We did not seek help in killing the prophets."
So you are testifying against yourselves, acknowledging that you are the sons of those who killed the two messengers.
